    "reasoning": "All eight mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. For q-167668, the function increases, has y-intercept -4, and approaches y=-3 from below; current option 0 depicts the same graph as the labeled solution image. For q-66509 and q-66514, only IV and III, respectively, pass the horizontal line test. For q-36941, only interval I is injective; II repeats heights across the central maximum, and III repeats heights on the outer branches. For q-36004, I and III are strictly increasing, while II contains increasing and decreasing portions with repeated heights. Its solution writes [-6,4] instead of the question's [-6,4); both fail injectivity, so this endpoint typo does not change the answer. For q-66725, slope -1 gives injectivity on every listed interval. For q-66669, the parabola is injective on either side of its vertex, but not on (-1,5). For q-141140, the graph crosses at -3 with nonzero slope, establishing a simple root. No submitted grades or earlier answers were provided; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
